Here's a similar problem I've been seeing; this one is semi-repeatable.

Hook up any old terminal to the serial port on the DS3100; configure it
in, log in on it, and run something that generates a decent amount of
output, e.g. "yes abcdefg".  Now go back to the DS3100 console, log in,
fire up a few windows and start clicking the mouse, bouncing between
windows, etc.  Very shortly, the machine should hang solidly.  I'd be
curious to know if anyone else has seen this one.

